   "what_g_bpnp_is": "BPnP.BPnP.forward returns P_6d = [rvec(3); t(3)] and BPnP.BPnP.backward returns dL/dpts2d = grad_output . d(rvec,t)/dpts2d.  So g_bpnp is the derivative of the **(rvec, t) parameter** vector w.r.t. the 2-D keypoints, contracted with the input perturbation.  Our paper's 6-DoF gradient is the **(omega, t_dot) tangent** vector (dR/dtheta=[omega]_x R); omega = J_l(w) w_dot.  The two bases agree only at w=0."
