   "verdict": "Setting the forward to the algebraic LS solution does NOT make the released backward consistent with it (rel=1.7e-01): both f=0 and grad C_alg=0 vanish there, but they are different systems, so their solution *maps* differ.  The released backward is nevertheless a correct IFT -- of its own f=0 system (rel=1.6e-07 vs FD of the f-root forward, 1.7e-07 vs the exact IFT of f).  The 17% is the depth weighting: f is the stationarity of sum_i S_i ||e_i||^2, the algebraic cost is sum_i ||r_i||^2 = sum_i S_i^2 ||e_i||^2; with the cube's depth spread of 0.61 the two maps differ by O(spread)."
